@@ -271,3 +271,55 @@ Custom fields can be scoped at three tiers:
 - **`SERVER` Scope:** Global fields available across all workspaces.
 
 **Dual-Control Governance:** Escalating a custom field definition from `PROJECT` to `WORKSPACE` or `SERVER` scope (or running with elevated Service Account credentials rather than `INVOKING_USER`) requires cryptographic approval by an administrator of that target tier with active Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2 / WebAuthn / TOTP) session elevation.
+
+---
+
+## Custom Field Configuration Attributes and Controls
+
+<a id="display-name"></a>
+### Display Name (`#display-name`)
+The human-readable title of the custom field shown on ticket property rails, board cards, and table columns.
+
+<a id="slug"></a>
+### Field Slug (`#slug`)
+The unique, URL-safe ASCII identifier used in formulas, API payloads, and query filters.
+
+<a id="flavors"></a>
+### Field Flavors (`#flavors`)
+Determines the underlying calculation mechanism: `scalar`, `formula`, `wasm`, or `nsjail`.
+
+<a id="sandbox-tier"></a>
+### Execution Sandbox Tier (`#sandbox-tier`)
+Selects between in-process WebAssembly (`wasmtime` Tier A) and containerized Linux namespaces (`nsjail` Tier B). In Standalone mode, `nsjail` is gated.
+
+<a id="credential-mode"></a>
+### Ephemeral Credential Mode (`#credential-mode`)
+Specifies whether the field executes with `INVOKING_USER` permissions or elevated `SERVICE_ACCOUNT` credentials.
+
+<a id="target-scope"></a>
+### Target Scope Tier (`#target-scope`)
+Controls the tenant boundary accessible to the custom field: `PROJECT`, `WORKSPACE`, or `SERVER`.
+
+<a id="output-formats"></a>
+### Output Formats (`#output-formats`)
+Canonical schema used to format and validate the output: `text`, `number`, `badge`, `severity_pill`, `url`, `markdown_snippet`, or `json_table`.
+
+<a id="format-metadata"></a>
+### Format Metadata Configuration (`#format-metadata`)
+JSON metadata configuring format-specific options such as decimal precision, color tokens, and table column schemas.
+
+<a id="script-source"></a>
+### Custom Script Source (`#script-source`)
+The Python AST expression, compiled WebAssembly module, or sandboxed script implementing the field calculation.
+
+<a id="egress-allowlist"></a>
+### Network Egress Allowlist (`#egress-allowlist`)
+Explicit list of destination hosts accessible to `nsjail` tier scripts. Network access is disabled by default via `CLONE_NEWNET`.
+
+<a id="aal2-stepup"></a>
+### Mandatory AAL2 Step-Up (`#aal2-stepup`)
+Administrative modifications and scope escalations require recent multi-factor authentication (AAL2 verified within 900 seconds).
+
+<a id="approvals"></a>
+### Dual-Control Cryptographic Approvals (`#approvals`)
+Escalating a field to workspace or server scope requires explicit cryptographic signing and approval by an administrator of that target tier.
