+## 10. Remote Runners Studio (`#runners-studio`)
+
+The Remote Runners Studio (`/admin/runners`) configures distributed build nodes, mints enrollment tokens, and monitors mTLS heartbeats.
+
+<a id="runners-configuration"></a>
+<a id="runners-studio"></a>
+
+### Remote Runners Studio Configuration Table
+
+| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| `runner_name` | Unique hostname or identifier of the runner node | String (1 to 64 characters) | Required | Displayed in runner health dashboard and active job telemetry |
+| `enrollment_token` | Single-use cryptographic token for runner registration | Base64-encoded HMAC string | Minted on demand | Expires after 60 minutes; grants certificate signing request (CSR) |
+| `mtls_cert_fingerprint`| SHA-256 fingerprint of validated client certificate | Hexadecimal SHA-256 hash | Registered upon enroll | Hardware-bound identity verifying mutual TLS WebSocket connection |
+| `max_concurrent_jobs` | Maximum simultaneous task executions allowed on runner | Integer between 1 and 16 | 2 | Throttles runner workload to prevent resource exhaustion |
+| `heartbeat_timeout_s` | Maximum allowable duration without ping before offline | Integer between 10 and 120 seconds | 30 | Dead runners are marked offline and active jobs rescheduled |
+| `allowed_repo_remotes` | Whitelist of Git repository URLs runner can clone | Comma-separated list of repository URLs | Empty (All authorized) | Prevents runner exploitation for arbitrary network exfiltration |
