+## 11. Standalone & Promotion Studio (`#standalone-studio`)
+
+The Standalone & Promotion Studio (`/admin/standalone`) inspects deployment topologies, triggers promotion to multi-container compose, and exports encrypted backups.
+
+<a id="standalone-configuration"></a>
+<a id="standalone-studio"></a>
+
+### Standalone & Promotion Studio Configuration Table
+
+| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| `deployment_mode` | Current platform runtime environment | `STANDALONE_CONTAINER`, `MULTI_CONTAINER_COMPOSE` | Detected at boot | Gates availability of nsjail container sandboxes and Redis hubs |
+| `backup_encryption_passphrase` | Secret passphrase used to derive AES-256 backup key | String (Minimum 16 characters) | User-supplied | Used by PBKDF2 to encrypt standalone archive into KBBAK1 format |
+| `target_postgres_url` | External database URL used during promotion cutover | Valid PostgreSQL connection string | None | Must support UTF-8, RLS, and required extensions (`ltree`, `pgvector`) |
+| `target_redis_url` | External Redis connection string for WebSocket pub/sub | Valid Redis URL (`redis://` or `rediss://`) | None | Decouples distributed realtime events from single-process memory |
+| `backup_storage_path` | Local filesystem path where backups are stored | Directory path (default `/var/backups/kanban`) | `/var/backups/kanban` | Requires write permissions; accessible for disaster recovery download |
+| `auto_promotion_verify` | Runs comprehensive post-migration verification suite | Boolean (`true` / `false`) | `true` | Asserts object link integrity and user access manifests before cutover |
